 "charts": [],
 "content": "[{\"id\": \"44be4d71a2\", \"type\": \"header\", \"data\": {\"text\": \"<span class='h4'><b>Stock &amp; Manufacturing</b></span>\", \"col\": 12}}, {\"id\": \"3bbc13a1a5\", \"type\": \"header\", \"data\": {\"text\": \"<span class='h4'><b>Shortcuts</b></span>\", \"col\": 12}}, {\"id\": \"5ccc0ca808\", \"type\": \"shortcut\", \"data\": {\"shortcut_name\": \"Stock Entry\", \"col\": 3}}, {\"id\": \"640a97f10f\", \"type\": \"shortcut\", \"data\": {\"shortcut_name\": \"Work Order\", \"col\": 3}}, {\"id\": \"4ea79e3241\", \"type\": \"shortcut\", \"data\": {\"shortcut_name\": \"Serial No\", \"col\": 3}}, {\"id\": \"404dfc0c20\", \"type\": \"shortcut\", \"data\": {\"shortcut_name\": \"Batch\", \"col\": 3}}, {\"id\": \"e096ad7ea7\", \"type\": \"shortcut\", \"data\": {\"shortcut_name\": \"Items\", \"col\": 3}}, {\"id\": \"3c2be536cc\", \"type\": \"spacer\", \"data\": {\"col\": 12}}, {\"id\": \"aa9d851111\", \"type\": \"header\", \"data\": {\"text\": \"<span class='h4'><b>Reports & Masters</b></span>\", \"col\": 12}}, {\"id\": \"4c613a551e\", \"type\": \"card\", \"data\": {\"card_name\": \"Manufacturing\", \"col\": 4}}, {\"id\": \"ba03f4d841\", \"type\": \"card\", \"data\": {\"card_name\": \"Stock Transactions\", \"col\": 4}}, {\"id\": \"dd013d7595\", \"type\": \"card\", \"data\": {\"card_name\": \"Stock Masters\", \"col\": 4}}, {\"id\": \"edc23956f0\", \"type\": \"card\", \"data\": {\"card_name\": \"Buying & Selling\", \"col\": 4}}, {\"id\": \"3d95993206\", \"type\": \"card\", \"data\": {\"card_name\": \"Stock Reports\", \"col\": 4}}, {\"id\": \"53ac35a9a5\", \"type\": \"card\", \"data\": {\"card_name\": \"Manufacturing Reports\", \"col\": 4}}, {\"id\": \"03adeb300e\", \"type\": \"spacer\", \"data\": {\"col\": 12}}, {\"id\": \"d40b58013a\", \"type\": \"header\", \"data\": {\"text\": \"<span class='h4'><b>How to use this screen</b></span>\", \"col\": 12}}, {\"id\": \"3607934eea\", \"type\": \"paragraph\", \"data\": {\"text\": \"<div style='border:1px solid var(--border-color);border-radius:8px;padding:14px 16px;background:var(--fg-color)'><p style='margin:0 0 6px'><b>How to use Stock &amp; Manufacturing</b></p><p style='margin:0 0 8px;color:var(--text-muted)'>The ERPNext side of the plant, in the order a pump is actually built: buy the components, melt and wind, raise a Work Order against a BOM, consume the batches, produce a serialised pump, test it, then dispatch it. Nothing here is a KUMAR invention - it is standard ERPNext, wired so the serial and batch numbers flow.</p><p style='margin:10px 0 4px'><b>Do this, in order</b></p><ol style='margin:0 0 4px 18px'><li><b>Item</b> - a finished pump has <i>Has Serial No</i> with the series <code>KP-&lt;MODEL&gt;-.YY..MM.-.#####</code>; casings, stators and rotors have <i>Has Batch No</i>. The <b>Traceability Group</b> field on the item is what tells the genealogy hook which slot a consumed part fills.</li><li><b>Purchase Order &rarr; Purchase Receipt</b> for bought-out parts (bearings, seals, capacitors). Supplier lots come in as batches.</li><li><b>BOM</b> then <b>Work Order</b> for a production run. Print the <b>Route Card</b> from the Work Order and let it travel with the job.</li><li><b>Stock Entry (Manufacture)</b> consumes the casing and stator batches and produces the pump. Serial numbers are generated here, and the heat and winding numbers are stamped onto each one automatically.</li><li><b>Pump Test Certificate</b> per unit, then <b>Delivery Note</b> / <b>Sales Invoice</b>. A unit that has not passed test cannot be delivered.</li><li><b>Stock Ledger</b>, <b>Stock Balance</b> and <b>Batch-wise Balance History</b> answer where anything is; <b>Serial No</b> answers what one unit is.</li></ol><p style='margin:10px 0 4px'><b>Watch out for</b></p><ul style='margin:0 0 4px 18px'><li>Do not type serials into the old text field - v16 keeps them in a Serial and Batch Bundle. Use the scan button or the bundle selector.</li><li>A Manufacture entry that consumes no traceable batch will warn you. Fix it before submitting; that gap cannot be filled in later.</li></ul></div>\", \"col\": 12}}]",
